NNAAMMEE
       dpkg-name - rename Debian packages to full package names

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddppkkgg--nnaammee [_o_p_t_i_o_n...]  [----] _f_i_l_e...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This manual page documents the ddppkkgg--nnaammee program which provides an easy
       way to rename DDeebbiiaann packages into their full package names. A full
       package name consists of _p_a_c_k_a_g_e___v_e_r_s_i_o_n___a_r_c_h_i_t_e_c_t_u_r_e.._p_a_c_k_a_g_e_-_t_y_p_e as
       specified in the control file of the package. The _v_e_r_s_i_o_n part of the
       filename consists of the upstream version information optionally
       followed by a hyphen and the revision information. The _p_a_c_k_a_g_e_-_t_y_p_e
       part comes from that field if present or fallbacks to ddeebb.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --aa, ----nnoo--aarrcchhiitteeccttuurree
           The destination filename will not have the architecture
           information.

       --kk, ----ssyymmlliinnkk
           Create a symlink, instead of moving.

       --oo, ----oovveerrwwrriittee
           Existing files will be overwritten if they have the same name as
           the destination filename.

       --ss, ----ssuubbddiirr [_d_i_r]
           Files will be moved into a subdirectory. If the directory given as
           argument exists the files will be moved into that directory
           otherwise the name of the target directory is extracted from the
           section field in the control part of the package. The target
           directory will be unstable/binary-_a_r_c_h_i_t_e_c_t_u_r_e/_s_e_c_t_i_o_n.  If the
           section is not found in the control, then nnoo--sseeccttiioonn is assumed,
           and in this case, as well as for sections nnoonn--ffrreeee and ccoonnttrriibb the
           target directory is _s_e_c_t_i_o_n/binary-_a_r_c_h_i_t_e_c_t_u_r_e.  The section field
           is not required so a lot of packages will find their way to the nnoo--
           sseeccttiioonn area.

           WWaarrnniinngg:: _U_s_e _t_h_i_s _o_p_t_i_o_n _w_i_t_h _c_a_r_e_, _i_t _i_s _m_e_s_s_y_.

       --cc, ----ccrreeaattee--ddiirr
           This option can used together with the --ss option. If a target
           directory isn't found it will be created automatically.

           WWaarrnniinngg:: _U_s_e _t_h_i_s _o_p_t_i_o_n _w_i_t_h _c_a_r_e_.

       --??, ----hheellpp
           Show the usage message and exit.

       --vv, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Show the version and exit.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       DDPPKKGG__CCOOLLOORRSS
           Sets the color mode (since dpkg 1.18.5).  The currently accepted
           values are: aauuttoo (default), aallwwaayyss and nneevveerr.

       DDPPKKGG__NNLLSS
           If set, it will be used to decide whether to activate Native
           Language Support, also known as internationalization (or i18n)
           support (since dpkg 1.19.0).  The accepted values are: 00 and 11
           (default).

BBUUGGSS
       Some packages don't follow the name structure
       _p_a_c_k_a_g_e___v_e_r_s_i_o_n___a_r_c_h_i_t_e_c_t_u_r_e..ddeebb.  Packages renamed by ddppkkgg--nnaammee will
       follow this structure. Generally this will have no impact on how
       packages are installed by ddsseelleecctt(1)/ddppkkgg(1), but other installation
       tools might depend on this naming structure.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       ddppkkgg--nnaammee bbaarr--ffoooo..ddeebb
           The file bbaarr--ffoooo..ddeebb will be renamed to bar-foo_1.0-2_i386.deb or
           something similar (depending on whatever information is in the
           control part of bbaarr--ffoooo..ddeebb).

       ffiinndd //rroooott//ddeebbiiaann// --nnaammee ''**..ddeebb'' || xxaarrggss --nn 11 ddppkkgg--nnaammee --aa
           All files with the extension ddeebb in the directory /root/debian and
           its subdirectory's will be renamed by ddppkkgg--nnaammee if required into
           names with no architecture information.

       ffiinndd --nnaammee ''**..ddeebb'' || xxaarrggss --nn 11 ddppkkgg--nnaammee --aa --oo --ss --cc
           DDoonn''tt ddoo tthhiiss..  Your archive will be messed up completely because a
           lot of packages don't come with section information.  DDoonn''tt ddoo
           tthhiiss..

       ddppkkgg--ddeebb ----bbuuiilldd ddeebbiiaann--ttmmpp &&&& ddppkkgg--nnaammee --oo --ss .... ddeebbiiaann--ttmmpp..ddeebb
           This can be used when building new packages.

